invariant: INV-11
file: hkdf.c
catches: hkdf384_test
reason: the dispatcher in hmac runs HMAC-SHA-256 for a hash_len of 48,
  so TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384's key schedule runs SHA-256 while its buffers
  and labels say SHA-384. Every secret it derives is then wrong, and a
  build that only exercised SHA-256 suites would not notice. The RFC 4231
  HMAC-SHA-384 vectors and the SHA-384 schedule rows in hkdf384_test go
  through hmac with hash_len 48, so they fail on the first derivation.

--- old
    if (hash_len == SHA384_LEN) {
        hmac_sha384(key, key_len, msg, msg_len, out);
        return;
    }
--- new
    if (hash_len == SHA384_LEN) {
        hmac_sha256(key, key_len, msg, msg_len, out);
        return;
    }
